@namespace Bit.BevTools.Demo.Client.Components

@* Where the sample is running right now. Under Interactive Auto the same page can come up on the
   Server renderer (a circuit) or on WebAssembly, and several scenarios behave differently on each,
   so every sample says which one it got. It takes no parameters, so a parent re-render never
   re-renders it: it adds nothing to the renders a scenario is about. *@

<span class="demo-renderer">
    <span class="bb-dot @(RendererInfo.IsInteractive ? "bb-dot-success" : "bb-dot-warning")" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    Renderer: <strong>@RendererInfo.Name</strong> · @(RendererInfo.IsInteractive ? "interactive" : "prerendering")
</span>
<span class="demo-shortcut"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd><kbd>D</kbd> opens BevTools</span>
